<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/sampling> skos:scopeNote "Use for quantized sample interpretation shared by raster, signal and point-cloud data. Precision, component organization and numeric interpretation are separate declarations."@en .
asamp:Float skos:definition "Sample interpretation using floating-point numeric values rather than integer quantization codes."@en .
asamp:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
asamp:SignedInteger skos:definition "Sample interpretation admitting negative and nonnegative integral values; precision is stated separately."@en .
asamp:UnsignedInteger skos:definition "Sample interpretation admitting only nonnegative integral values; precision is stated separately."@en .
